<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Compagnie de l'Orient</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1642–1664</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as French Company of the East</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Compagnie de l'Orient was a French trading company chartered in 1642 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardinal-richelieu">Cardinal Richelieu</a> to trade and found colonies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, especially in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>. It sent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-pronis">Jacques Pronis</a> to found <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taolagnaro">Fort-Dauphin</a> in south-east Madagascar in 1643, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etienne-de-flacourt">Étienne de Flacourt</a> later governed the post. Short of capital and troubled by conflict with the Malagasy, it was absorbed into the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-east-india-company">French East India Company</a> in 1664.</p></div>
